{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-descartes-elliptic-curve","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:descartes-elliptic-curve","kind":"proposition","title":"The Descartes elliptic curve $\\mathcal{E}_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-color-tube-cubic"],"tags":["elliptic-curve","descartes","color-fibration","substrate-parameter","golden-ratio","weierstrass"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_elliptic_curve","text":"descartes-elliptic-curve.md","leanSource":"descartes-elliptic-curve.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:descartes-elliptic-curve\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be the Descartes universe with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_{\\mathrm{eu}}(M_0) = -6</code> and substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>. Set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s = \\sqrt{q}</code>. The fibrewise color curve <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{E}_z\\colon y^2=F(X,z)</code> (<a href=\"#prop:color-elliptic\" data-at=\"brings-surface/color-fibration-elliptic\">color elliptic</a>) of Bring's surface at spacetime ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = s - s^{-1}</code> is the elliptic curve</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{E}_q  : \n  y^2 =  x^3\n  +  \\frac{2s^4 + s^3 - 2s^2 - s + 2}{3s^2}x\n  +  \\frac{5(s^2 + s - 1)(4s^4 - s^3 - 4s^2 + s + 4)}{27s^3}</code></pre>\n<p>with Weierstrass coefficients expressible directly in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  p(q) = \n  \\frac{2(q^2 - q + 1)}{3q}\n  +  \\frac{q - 1}{3\\sqrt{q}},</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  r(q) = \n  \\frac{20(q - 1)^3}{27q^{3/2}}\n  +  \\frac{5(q - 1)^2}{9q}\n  +  \\frac{5(\\sqrt{q} - 1/\\sqrt{q})}{9}\n  +  \\frac{20}{27}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"8.8.15","page":"b/prop-descartes-elliptic-curve","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.descartes_elliptic_curve","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-elliptic-curve.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
